{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/345761-confused-about-combat","id":345761,"title":"Confused about Combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-20T07:55:18-08:00","id":345761,"title":"Confused about Combat","content":"Been reading through the book, and I remain fairly confused as to how an average combat round goes. This is what I've grasped, is it right?<br /> <br /> 1. Everyone rolls a d10, adding their Dex and Wits. Order of turns goes in descending order.<br /> 2. Say Person A wants to punch Person B. They then roll their Brawl (or Martial Arts if they're being fancy): not their Dexterity + Brawl, like other WW games, just Brawl. They want dice to show 7+, and one or more of these dice means A has hit B, like with nWoD. Extra dice adds to damage. If B is actively defending, it's an opposed roll, with B rolling whatever ability makes sense for how they're defending. Again, just the ability. Barring Enhancements, Mega Attributes don't really come into this stage in any meaningful way.<br /> 3. Say A hits. A now grabs a number of dice equal to the listed damage for how they hit B, usually Strength plus something, plus additional successes on the attack roll. They then subtract the targets relevant soak from this dice pool, and roll whatever is left, rolling one if none are left. Mega Strength may affect this stage if suitable. B says ow if A rolls any dice showing 7+.<br /> <br /> Is that more or less how it goes? I've played WW games before, mostly nWoD, and the description here isn't as clear as I'm used to in other games. I know there's lots of house rules people use, and that's cool. But I need to grasp the fundamental system before I start messing with it too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:40:31-08:00","id":345965,"title":"","content":"You do still add your Strength (with Brawl) or Dexterity (with Martial Arts) to the basic attack pool, but you've got the gist otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T16:46:22-08:00","id":346234,"title":"","content":"Allan53, I think that it was not quite clear. Each Ability is paired with an Attribute. If you look at the sample character sheet, then you will note that each Ability is under an Attribute. So you pair the Ability with the Attribute it is under (in most cases. Some exceptions do apply) and that is the dice pool you roll when told to make a Brawl or Martial Art or Athletics roll.<br /> Additionally, Mega-Attributes can affect the target number and bring it below 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T16:59:33-08:00","id":346238,"title":"","content":"I assumed that was because if you have zero points in the Ability in question, you used that attribute instead? Which now I think about it would be kind of silly, a person with, say, 3 Strength would need 4 Brawl before they're rolling better than they would be if they had no training. Which is dumb, so probably wrong.<br /> <br /> But if that's the case, then wouldn't the balance be kind of heavily skewed towards the attacker, all else being equal? I mean, if you're just rolling 2 dice for your 2 points in Brawl, then you'd expect one success per roll, more or less. But if you're throwing say 2 Strength and 2 Brawl, you'd expecting just under 2, which'd make combat reasonably lethal? I suppose the idea for most is just to beat people down, rather than kill.<br /> <br /> Lemme just run the numbers through. Say a person with 2 Strength and 2 Brawl punches someone with the same stats. A is throwing 4 dice, barring Mega-Attributes. Say B isn't actively defending. A gets, say, 2 successes. So they then work out their dice pool of 3 (2 Strength plus one for extra successes). They then remove B's soak, which we'll say is 2 for his 2 Stamina since it's just bashing damage. A is now throwing 1 dice for damage, all else being equal.<br /> <br /> Huh. I guess that is pretty balanced, at least in theory.Kind of Scion-ish, in that it gets whittled pretty quick down the process.<br /> <br /> I get Mega-Attributes make this more complicated, but say A has 1 point in Mega-Strength, and they apply their point into an extra Mega-dice, and it doesn't work out. It happens. Can they then apply that point again to damage, in addition to the passive benefit of adding extra damage just from the MS? On the one hand, it is a different roll, but it's part of the same action. Either way. Damn. Don't get into a punching fight with a MStr guy unless you've got a way of dealing with his damage output.<br /> <br /> <i>EDIT: Hey, 500 posts. Cool for me.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/345761-confused-about-combat?p=346234#post346234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, Mega-Attributes can affect the target number and bring it below 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't they affect difficulty, which is number of successes, not target number? You gain additional benefits for a successful Mega dice, but the target number is described as being the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 12-20-2014, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T21:11:00-08:00","id":346433,"title":"","content":"I apologize. I meant target number. As far as the Mega-Strength, the extra successes are passive. You get those but you do not get the chance to lower the target number, nor do you get the chance to roll Mega-Strength to get extra successes, either. <br /> Combat cab get pretty scary in Aberrant and wild an wooly, but it is balanced out by the powers and Mega-Attributes. With the various powers and Mega-Attribute Enhancements, offence and defense is more even sided. Tough Man can be made that is almost impossible to hurt physically, but that is why there are not as many mental defenses. So forth and so on. It is a game of Rock-Paper-Scissors when it comes down to it. Find out where the person is weakest and hit them like that. It is why a group is good to have that is varied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T23:37:43-08:00","id":348061,"title":"","content":"I do not actually remember any effect in Aberrant that would affect Target Number but Mega Attributes can be used to reduce the difficulty, ie the number of success needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T15:09:44-08:00","id":355168,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Trinity Universe was the first of the WW games to have a static target number. It doesn't change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T17:26:45-08:00","id":356112,"title":"","content":"Mega-Stamina is also massively overshadowed by Mega-Strength. Mega-Stamina 5 without Enhancements might be able to deflect some assault rifle fire. Mega-Strength 5 without Enhancements pulps anything made of flesh and even one dot in Mega-Strength can allow a nova to do serious damage to a tank, potentially using a Smackdown attack to wreck it in one hit. In comparison, Mega-Stamina 1 struggles to make gunshots from the smallest of small arms more survivable, and you certainly wouldn't be able to take a hit from the tank that a Mega-Strength 1 nova could total as easily as a certain other game's &quot;Mercer&quot; character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T21:19:17-08:00","id":356236,"title":"","content":"I haven't actually played the game, but favouring offense seems like a wise move if you're going to favour one side. Exalted favours defense, and the issues for that are well documented. So favouring offense means, at least, that stuff happens in combat. Just my thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T12:15:35-08:00","id":357649,"title":"","content":"For Clarity: With Str 2 and Brawl 2, you roll 4 dice. Success is a 7 (or higher) on each die. And In the Original Aberrant, Mega-Strength 1, would give either, -1 Difficulty OR +1 Die to the attack pool. AND a +5 Auto successes on your Damage roll.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T17:55:59-08:00","id":357923,"title":"","content":"And that die gives one more success on a successful roll than a normal dice would (2 on a 7-9, 3 on a 10), which I'm pretty sure would stack with the Damage bonus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T22:48:09-08:00","id":358067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Clarity: With Str 2 and Brawl 2, you roll 4 dice. Success is a 7 (or higher) on each die. And In the Original Aberrant, Mega-Strength 1, would give either, -1 Difficulty OR +1 Die to the attack pool. AND a +5 Auto successes on your Damage roll. </div> </div> </div>Actually no.<br /> <br /> Mega-Strength works differently from any other Mega-Attribute, it mentions this in it's description. Mega-Strength never gives difficulty reductions nor extra dice for pools but what it does is give the Automatic successes, 5 per level of Mega-Strength, on many strength/might rolls and to close combat damage pools.<br /> <br /> So for clarity: With Str 2 and Brawl 2, you roll 4 dice. Success is a 7 (or higher) on each die. And in the Original Aberrant, Mega-Strength 1, would give 5 Auto successes on your Damage roll. In situations like Grappling it works like competing Mega-Attributes and makes Mega-Strength Novas absolute monsters in such situations. All this works to balance Mega-Strength a bit in that it doesn't make it easier to hit your target but it does mean that if you hit you'll do absolutely ridiculous damage. This of course is can be circumvented by being a Martial Artist who does roll his Dex+MA+ either Mega-Dex dice and/or Difficulty reduction from Mega-Dex and still adds Meg-Strength to damage pools in the end, as it is still a close combat damage pool where Mega-Strength specifically works as automatic successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T23:38:28-08:00","id":358075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/345761-confused-about-combat?p=358067#post358067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually no.<br /> <br /> Mega-Strength works differently from any other Mega-Attribute, it mentions this in it's description. Mega-Strength never gives difficulty reductions nor extra dice for pools but what it does is give the Automatic successes, 5 per level of Mega-Strength, on many strength/might rolls and to close combat damage pools.<br /> <br /> So for clarity: With Str 2 and Brawl 2, you roll 4 dice. Success is a 7 (or higher) on each die. And in the Original Aberrant, Mega-Strength 1, would give 5 Auto successes on your Damage roll. In situations like Grappling it works like competing Mega-Attributes and makes Mega-Strength Novas absolute monsters in such situations. All this works to balance Mega-Strength a bit in that it doesn't make it easier to hit your target but it does mean that if you hit you'll do absolutely ridiculous damage. This of course is can be circumvented by being a Martial Artist who does roll his Dex+MA+ either Mega-Dex dice and/or Difficulty reduction from Mega-Dex and still adds Meg-Strength to damage pools in the end, as it is still a close combat damage pool where Mega-Strength specifically works as automatic successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, if you're up against a target with an armor add, the automatic successes and the armor add both disappear and you just subtract soak from damage. A main battle tank has soak 6, so with a Smackdown attack, you can roll your Strength + extra attack successes in damage. If you have Claws, you can slash apart the most heavily armored vehicles in one or two typical hits.<br /> <br /> Just to re-emphasize, Mega-Strength 1 allows you to beat a nova with Mega-Stamina 1 to death without even thinking about it. A single mitoid can end a supposedly super-tough nova without even trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T00:13:28-08:00","id":358079,"title":"","content":"Mitoid? Google isn't being helpful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T12:21:09-08:00","id":358497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/345761-confused-about-combat?p=358079#post358079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mitoid? Google isn't being helpful</div> </div> </div> </div>'Mitoid' Is the colloquial term for users of the drug Mite, which can give a baseline human a single level of Mega-Strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T20:36:54-08:00","id":409567,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the game does tend to be a bit unbalanced in terms of favouring damage over soak, which can lead to problems with lethality. As well as making tank characters less viable (especially with minimum damage, although the optional errata thing in the player's guide helps with that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3355-not-a-platypus","name":"Not a Platypus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T04:29:38-08:00","id":416350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Not a Platypus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/345761-confused-about-combat?p=409567#post409567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the game does tend to be a bit unbalanced in terms of favouring damage over soak, which can lead to problems with lethality. As well as making tank characters less viable (especially with minimum damage, although the optional errata thing in the player's guide helps with that).</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Where? I've been looking in the book all afternoon and can't find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}